{
  "kind": "Panel",
  "spec": {
    "id": 62,
    "title": "Threads views, link clicks & engagement ${chart}",
    "description": "Per day (time ranges over 7 days): Views from Threads (through Postiz, the last 30 days at each poll, kept); Link clicks = taps on links in your posts (from Threads with the channel's token, needs POSTIZ_DB_PASSWORD). The thin dashed line is each day's number, the bold one the 7-day average (of the days the bridge has among the 7 ending that day; it starts once 4 of them are there): the trend, through the day-to-day ups and downs. Violet lines are this network's posts: hover one to see what went out; a rise just after one is that post working. Hour by hour (when the time range is 7 days or less): what came in between the bridge's checks (about once an hour; a point after a gap covers the gap), no 7-day line. Kept for the last 90 days (ACCOUNT_CHECK_DAYS); further back, pick per day. Both follow the dashboard's time range. Views and link clicks come only per day, so the bridge keeps today's so far (UTC) at each check and the point is the difference. Engagement (blue) = likes, replies, reposts and quotes added up, from Threads' account insights (with POSTIZ_DB_PASSWORD; else through Postiz, the last 30 days at each poll); every day kept; hover for each, and for the engagement rate: the 7 days' engagement as a share of the 7 days' views, comparable between networks. Engagement has its own scale, on the right (it's usually a small share of the views): lines moving together = a steady rate; engagement rising faster = posts landing better, slower = more people seeing them but fewer joining in. Hour by hour, engagement is what all your posts gained between checks (each post's numbers when it's checked: the newest every check, older ones in turn), since the account's numbers for a day keep coming in after it ends; it has no rate.",
    "links": [],
